# kernel-bfin.img -- Linux 4.9.156 for the ADSP-BF537 (Blackfin, noMMU)
#
# Runs on qemu-system-bfin -M bf537-stamp from the qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
# branch uclibc-ng); upstream qemu never had Blackfin.  The image is the
# stripped vmlinux (ELF), which the machine loads and starts in the reset
# event with the command line in R0, as the boot loader would.
#
#   qemu-system-bfin -M bf537-stamp -m 256M -nographic -kernel kernel-bfin.img \
#     -initrd rootfs.img.xz -append console=ttyBF0,57600
#
# -m 256M: the unpacked FLAT test rootfs is about 117 MB and lives in RAM.
# The STAMP has 64 MiB and the BF537's controller goes to 128 MiB; the machine
# reports 256 MiB through EBIU_SDBCTL with the encoding of the larger parts,
# which is where Linux takes its memory size from.
#
# -initrd: Blackfin Linux had no way to be handed an initrd.  The machine
# loads the image below the uncached DMA area at the top of memory and appends
# "initrd=start,size" to the command line; kernel-bfin-initrd.patch teaches
# the kernel to read it and reserve the area, as arm and arc do.
#
# Build: kernel-bfin.config is BF537-STAMP_defconfig with
#   - the serial driver in PIO mode on UART0 as console
#   - no MTD, SPI, I2C, sound, watchdog or Ethernet (the machine has none)
#   - DEVTMPFS, SIGNALFD, TIMERFD, BLK_DEV_INITRD with an empty
#     INITRAMFS_SOURCE
#   - CMDLINE_BOOL off: a built-in command line would replace the one in R0
#   - BFIN_EXTMEM_ICACHEABLE off: with it, anomaly 05000263 caps the usable
#     memory at 60 MB; the machine models no caches anyway
#
#   cd linux-4.9.156
#   patch -p1 < kernel-bfin-initrd.patch
#   cp kernel-bfin.config .config
#   make ARCH=blackfin CROSS_COMPILE=bfin-openadk-uclinux-uclibc- \
#        HOSTCFLAGS=-fcommon olddefconfig vmlinux
#   bfin-openadk-uclinux-uclibc-strip -o kernel-bfin.img vmlinux
#
# HOSTCFLAGS=-fcommon because 4.9's dtc does not build with gcc >= 10 otherwise.
# 4.9 is the newest usable kernel: arch/blackfin was removed in v4.17.
#
# Result with the CI's FLAT rootfs: 341 passed, 0 failed, 16 skipped in about
# 2.5 minutes.
